# Shell scripts and container files must stay LF: a Windows clone with core.autocrlf=true would otherwise
# COPY a CRLF entrypoint into the image and boot fails with `/bin/sh^M: bad interpreter` (a lesson borrowed
# from SillyTavern's Dockerfile, which dos2unix's its entrypoint at build time instead).
*.sh          text eol=lf
Dockerfile    text eol=lf
*.yaml        text eol=lf
*.yml         text eol=lf
*.env         text eol=lf
*.env.example text eol=lf
